<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Saudi Arabia says it will retaliate after deadly Houthi attacks on airports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9f295ce4492476dc4af891114b4aadfb6dbf23a78d7d880dd0fed09bd2eaa0e</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T03:02:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261008-saudi-arabia-strikes-deadly-houthi-attacks-airports" /><summary type="html">Saudi authorities said Wednesday three people were killed and 36 wounded in attacks on Abha and Riyadh’s King Khalid international airports claimed by Yemen’s Iran-backed Houthis. The Saudi-led coalition said it destroyed the ballistic missile launch platform used to attack Riyadh, as fighting with the Houthis intensified across the region.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>No longer the same Israel? October 7th and the future of the Jewish State</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5e42fcc8f249541d43769440299f5f204b55ad7179690c5d0896dd6d01b9130</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T22:10:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261007-no-longer-the-same-israel-october-7th-and-the-future-of-the-jewish-state" /><summary type="html">For now, it's still Benjamin Netanyahu’s Israel. In 2023, in the immediate aftermath of the country’s worst day of bloodshed in its history, pundits predicted the quick demise of the right wing prime minister. On this the third anniversary of the October Seventh attacks, Israel’s still not reckoned with the security failures on the day, the root causes of the Hamas-led terror attack, the brutal war of vengeance that followed and most of all, Netanyahu’s still prime minister with a fair shot at re-election. Even if the Likud leader’s voted out on October 27th, his most serious general election rivals don't exactly advocate for a radical break when it comes to the Palestinians.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>Israel marks three years since October 7 attack ahead of elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ca682dc339063fd7891e332899cbd5d4fbf63be6fd35f673b722b3024de99da</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T21:50:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-three-years-october-7-attack-elections" /><summary type="html">Israel marked the third anniversary of Hamas’s October 7 attack on Wednesday with silent tributes and renewed strikes on Gaza as political debate intensified ahead of elections. Families gathered at the Nova festival site and Kfar Aza kibbutz. Gaza officials said strikes killed five people despite a year-old ceasefire agreement.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'It's still unclear whether Netanyahu will pay for what happened during his time in office'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc82756fc95f2050c9da4060ead6f0b26af8fe5a0b633c255202dafe186af1d3</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T19:52:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/it-s-still-unclear-whether-netanyahu-will-pay-for-what-happened-during-his-time-in-office" /><summary type="html">As Israel marks the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks, questions linger about the warnings Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu received about them. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Ayala Panievsky, Lecturer at City University of London and author of The New Censorship, explains that the allegations in the run-up to the elections "are very damaging for Netanyahu but there are some factors mitigating the risk for him", including a fragmented opposition as well as the control of major media.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Resilience' of Israelis as they mourn the loss of loved ones and 'the sense that we can be safe'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cd0c4da78991f3a86ce620178745b0fe1d64ef8d80bbcc37036c524cdf8a447</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T17:46:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-resilience-of-israelis-as-they-the-mourn-loss-of-loved-ones-and-the-sense-that-we-can-be-safe" /><summary type="html">Angela Diffley is pleased to welcome Dr. Danny Brom, Founding Director of METIV, the Israel Psychotrauma Center in Jerusalem. According to Dr. Brom, as Israelis and Jewish people around the world continue to mourn the largest loss of Jewish life on a single day since the Holocaust, their fundamental sense of collective security has also been shattered. What strikes him, however, is the resilience that exists alongside the grieving. How can individuals, communities and society rebuild a sense of safety without allowing fear to dictate the future? Yet, as Dr. Brom observes, “the war is still going on,” while political leaders speak of pursuing “the ultimate victory, which no one really knows what that is.”</summary></entry><entry><title>October 7: Former Israeli hostage speaks to France 24</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:902aa817527805103196364a19ae45f4342875aacf96bfffc92140111968650e</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:30:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-former-israeli-hostage-speaks-to-france-24" /><summary type="html">“The terrorists pulled us out through the window. They handcuffed me and pushed us into a car that they had brought from Gaza.”
 
Former Israeli hostage Shoshan Haran speaks to France 24.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Time doesn't heal': Parents of October 7 attacks victim Aner Shapira</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a23921d961aaf5516126dac944fef737c873399399df084835d51f1633d55d8a</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T12:59:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261007-time-doesn-t-heal-parents-of-aner-shapira-killed-on-october-7-2023" /><summary type="html">The parents of a 22-year-old Israeli man who was killed when Hamas attacked the Nova music festival on October 7, 2023 have told FRANCE 24 how they can still feel him surrounding them even though he's no longer here. Shira and Moshe Shapira say that time doesn't heal, but they are learning how to live with their loss. Their son Aner managed to throw seven grenades back towards Hamas fighters, before an eighth exploded in his hands, killing him. They spoke to us in Perspective.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>October 7: Israelis mark three years since Hamas attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cd4a68f70613d9ad4c25d1381b80ba54528f0bc9b7eafbf9148302501a5e04f6</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T11:04:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261007-october-7-israelis-mark-three-years-since-hamas-attacks" /><summary type="html">Israel is marking the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023, Hamas terrorist attack on Wednesday with memorials across the country.
 
At the site of the Nova music festival, where more than 300 people were killed, families gathered at dawn for a moment of silence and paid tribute in front of portraits both of festival-goers and security forces who died on October 7.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli papers commemorate October 7 attacks, three years on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91b0fd9b292b415e24ea0d8d675dbe1834ec8f671f8d04fe70a200e5aff9ebef</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T10:55:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261007-israeli-papers-commemorate-october-7-attacks-three-years-on" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, October 7: Papers mark the third anniversary of the October 7 attacks. But first: the high school protests that have swept across France make the front pages at home and abroad. Also, the Argentinian press waves off Lionel Messi after his last international match. Finally, a British adventurer completes a 28-year walk around the world.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>How Netanyahu survived the political fallout from the October 7 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4aff0b63ae400967e04d7a66160bbe91baa372eb8bf086e23b18a3a5a5098861</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T05:24:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-how-netanyahu-survived-the-political-fallout-from-the-october-7-attacks" /><summary type="html">Three years after the deadly Hamas-led October 7 attacks in southern Israel, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu is fighting for political survival ahead of legislative elections later this month. Reports that Arab leaders warned him of the assault in advance have undercut his claims that Israel's security chiefs are to blame, but his political base appears to be holding.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French FM denounces 'poison' of anti-Semitism as Israel marks October 7 attacks anniversary</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:385f837ede0f32b1f7096e22d0e3eecd8f81698a3d5f6107b5d2a24d87dd4c8b</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:46:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-middle-east-live-houthis-target-airport-in-yemen-as-israel-marks-october-7-anniversary" /><summary type="html">Israelis on Wednesday took part in commemorations for the victims of Hamas's October 7, 2023 attacks, which killed 1,200 people and saw 251 hostages taken. French Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot denounced the "poison of anti-Semitism" as he attended a memorial ceremony at the site of the Nova music festival massacre. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel marks third anniversary of October 7 attack as election looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d59dfb5e26774f68860735379fb14cd6396968951bbbe0f1b3544cdc750540f1</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T02:14:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261007-israel-marks-third-anniversary-of-october-7-attack-as-election-looms" /><summary type="html">Israel will mark the third anniversary of the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack on Wednesday with memorial events across the country, as heightened security surrounds the commemorations and voters prepare for an election in which the deadliest day in Israel’s history is expected to remain a central issue.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'We were naive' about Hamas, Israeli ex-hostage Shoshan Haran says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ba8fe299cf6c98477d31df4dc2a04b567bd369a1f0112f30b26f58376a06039</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T15:01:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says--83490e71ebdf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israeli former hostage Shoshan Haran said "we were naive" about Hamas before the October 7, 2023 attack on her kibbutz. Held in Gaza for 50 days, she recalled refusing to "show weakness" to her captors. She also called the accusations of genocide against Israel "a lie" and shared her late husband's last words.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Israel warns Gazans will pay 'heavy price' for any October 7 attacks on military</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78151262b5106560a7561def331a198ab03d52f56366c17f64bc8018f16b7aec</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T07:50:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military--16171ff124a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military" /><summary type="html">Israel on Tuesday said that Hamas and the Palestinian population in Gaza would pay a "heavy price" if any of Israel's armed forces were harmed on the three-year anniversary of the militant group's October 7 attack.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi-backed Yemeni forces expel the Houthis from several areas around key strait, officials say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e1ec83c99fdc48476d2f1b66a83493b95debe8766024e03e599edd1fe62ac6d</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:17:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say--6def5d5b3087.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say" /><summary type="html">Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces staged a lightning advance on ​Monday to retake the coast around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait up to the city of Mocha, the government said, pushing the Iran-backed Houthis out of most of the areas they seized last month. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b6d4e0c95910bea3e261c3a7c6710be036d062590529de5f848ba83b0dab75f</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:46:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-c--177d80f183d4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim attacks on Riyadh airport as Saudi-led forces strike Yemen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbcf76cfd9879bbd7a9829736bf53d33c5ccf9bf0793a3ae1570b08ae41108dc</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T08:12:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-terri--eb1150ba341e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-territory" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthis said Monday they had struck Riyadh's international airport and an Aramco refinery as Saudi-led forces intensified attacks on Houthi positions in Yemen in a bid to retake territory. Pakistan and Turkey also pledged troops to Saudi Arabia under a new defence pact.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran says no military solution to war as peace talks with US stall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b0caf7302dc8b3c0ccef55151fd3dad022a8f2554b225148bd744ad4c1de8de</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T21:41:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks--489f2da42d26.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks" /><summary type="html">Iran's diplomat said on Sunday there was no military solution to the US war against Iran as peace talks appeared stalled. Washington has scaled back attacks in favour of economic pressure, while Iran's attempted Hormuz blockade remains contentious. A UK maritime agency reported another tanker hit by an unidentified projectile.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: Disaster averted on Flydubai flight, French school protests and Bangkok floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcfae6a72e3052d2e3e2482c7400f159e2a710edadef9ef95d78a2c269907edd</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T13:35:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-fl--aacc58ef2e53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-floods" /><summary type="html">From French highschoolers protesting to demand better learning conditions to a Flydubai flight diverted to Saudi Arabia after a flightcrew member's onboard attack and flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's government declares counter-offensive as Houthis cut vital route to besieged city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9f1a299b7c506328b1857e84a8ea859e45adc7126734e2298bab332a502a452</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz--d567521fb6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz" /><summary type="html">The ​leader of ​Yemen's Saudi-backed government announced the beginning of a ​major ‌military ⁠operation against the Iran-backed Houthis ‌on Sunday aimed at ⁠recapturing territory under their control. The announcement came as Houthi forces cut off a vital supply route to the besieged government-held city of Taiz, according to several security sources.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Palestinians ‘harassed’ by settlers’ increasing use of drones</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4617e975025bab0e42df7c71ae4fab92d82880fa6e75293c53d11ca84d7a714</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T12:01:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones--66a927f7344d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones" /><summary type="html">Palestinians and activists report an increased use of drones in the occupied West Bank, particularly by the army and settlers, to whom the government supplies the drones directly. The drones are used to intimidate, monitor, demolish and make daily life unbearable.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel prepares to mark October 7</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7895beb260e2d7b95ca83ba10fbd0876290681930fd2aa37b7ad508bd2826b00</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T10:59:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7--474582fa3044.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7" /><summary type="html">An Israeli strike on a civilian vehicle in Gaza on Sunday killed one Palestinian and wounded at least 11 others. Israel’s military said it was targeting a Hamas militant. Palestinians have reported a surge in Israeli fire and airstrikes across Gaza over the past month, with more than 75,000 people killed and much of the enclave destroyed. Meanwhile, Israelis held their weekly protest in Tel Aviv’s Hostages Square, the last before Wednesday marks three years since the October 7 attack. Protesters said they wanted to commemorate the victims and demand an independent state inquiry into the events and decisions that led to the attack. The Hamas-led assault killed around 1,200 people in Israel and saw more than 250 others taken hostage, according to Israeli authorities. Rachael Goldberg Polin, an American-Israeli activist and mother of slain hostage Hersh Goldberg-Polin, speaks to France 24.</summary></entry><entry><title>Who are the mystery pilots who successfully landed endangered Flydubai flight 1073?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f5f311eab3d43f9f9de0edda3045bfa0efc886c59029d5e66d3d13f74c3986eb</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T09:36:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-who-are-the-mystery-pilots-who-successfully-landed-endangered-flydubai-flight-1073--a72a1f7feac2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-who-are-the-mystery-pilots-who-successfully-landed-endangered-flydubai-flight-1073" /><summary type="html">A passenger on Flydubai flight 1073 has described the actions of on-duty crew members who rushed into the cockpit to stabilise and land the plane after the co-pilot attacked the captain with a crash axe. The flight carrying 182 people en route to Israel Wednesday was able to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen’s Houthis claim attacks on Aramco facilities in Riyadh</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4636d234b095858b5192489c9c5f2f3974da51146eb3c146efa07928a3c11521</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T08:21:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-attacks-on-aramco-facilities-in-riyadh--5e9c9bc16a48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-attacks-on-aramco-facilities-in-riyadh" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Houthi rebels have claimed responsibility for attacks in Riyadh, including on facilities belonging to Aramco, the world’s largest oil company. This follows reports from residents of flames and smoke rising from an oil facility on the outskirts of the Saudi capital. Meanwhile, the Houthis have accused Saudi Arabia of launching dozens of strikes on Sanaa, warning that they will continue to respond to any escalation with further escalation. Here’s Jennie Shin with more on the situation on the ground.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis claim strike on oil facilty near Riyadh, accuse Saudi forces of pounding Yemen's capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9cd59b32e9134116044912c2177d6e5838a6bef1f45b771f934e3dd7c705a1e0</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T14:31:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa--81b4ce29f4be.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa" /><summary type="html">Houthi rebels accused Saudi forces of launching 26 strikes on Sanaa on Saturday after loud explosions rocked the Yemeni capital. The Iran-backed group said it struck an oil facility south of Riyadh, where flames and a large plume of smoke were seen rising from a plant belonging to oil giant Aramco.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UAE investigators say Omani Flydubai co-pilot was planning 'terrorist' attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:941a3551bbd31a009e79799dcdb2b48e94aaec46b8ffc8ddf0499bf3135a60f6</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:17:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views--d42f7d08990d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views" /><summary type="html">The Omani co-pilot accused of attacking the captain aboard a Flydubai flight to Israel on September 30 attempted to carry out a "terrorist" attack, the United Arab Emirates prosecutor general said ​Saturday. The alleged assailant, identified as Omani national Hamam al-Hammami, had been barred from flying in his country due to his radical ideological views, several media reported.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu warns of 'very heavy price' if any country found to be behind FlyDubai incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:152f5744f67a1997387e625188d8f5edb8150f81f114ea43941851801ede86a2</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T13:55:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident--ca93f0f1308d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday warned that any country or organisation found to be responsible for the violent clash on board an Israel-bound FlyDubai flight would "pay a very heavy price". While Netanyahu has alleged the co-pilot who stabbed his captain mid-flight had undergone "Islamist radicalisation", the motive behind the incident remains unclear.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>'America is leaving Iraq, but Iran isn't: Withdrawal a massive strategic and tactical mistake'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8bcd3cff8ff487170e98a92edf0bc91ea06e6f8bf4c44784679a3dd8f8748b2f</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T10:11:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake---0b781c6b753d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bamo Nouri, investigative journalist and also Honorary Research Fellow with the Department of International Politics at City Saint George's University of London. He sees the end of the American military presence in Iraq as a profound shift in the balance of power inside the country. For him, the central question is not whether Iraq has formally regained sovereignty, but whether it possesses the political cohesion, security capacity and economic independence necessary to exercise that sovereignty.</summary></entry><entry><title>Flydubai hero pilot tells Modi 'I could not let all those people die'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6c13690d6b454f525d3832c49eaaeb54c4f7f9a02909126daa6238097546ad9</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T09:04:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-flydubai-hero-pilot-tells-modi-i-could-not-let-all-those-people-die--42220aab298b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-flydubai-hero-pilot-tells-modi-i-could-not-let-all-those-people-die" /><summary type="html">Smit Machchhar, the Indian captain who was attacked by his co-pilot onboard the Flydubai flight 1073 in an apparent attempt to crash the plane, on Friday told Prime Minister Narendra Modi that although he was severely injured in the altercation, “I could not let all those people die”. Although collapsed, he made a last-ditch effort and managed to push the door to the cockpit open.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Egypt warned Israel of 'major' Hamas attack: 'No world where Netanyahu's not aware' (Vivian Salama)</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c403da6327c43739528fc0f2d3e48b999bb84c88147c5c510df6965cd7f8422a</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T06:08:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-egypt-warned-israel-of-major-hamas-attack-no-world-where-netanyahu-s-not-aware-vivian-salam--f8a90c764c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261002-egypt-warned-israel-of-major-hamas-attack-no-world-where-netanyahu-s-not-aware-vivian-salama" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Vivian Salama from Washington. An attorney and staff writer at The Atlantic, Salama has reported from more than 85 countries. Her latest investigation takes us back to September 26, 2023. As Israel's national security establishment gathered to commemorate the 50th anniversary of the Yom Kippur War and one of the country's greatest intelligence failures, Abbas Kamel, then Egypt's intelligence chief, made an exceptionally rare and discreet visit to Israel with a stark warning about the dangerous situation unfolding in Gaza.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry></feed>
